{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Prints the whole SONG chain of a TT-303PATGEN instance (all cells, with their repeats) as one real MIDI item, so a finished arrangement of the eight slots becomes a fixed track. Turn on SEQ LINK in TT-303PATGEN first, select the target track, put the edit cursor where the item should start and run the script. It asks how many times the chain is printed in a row (1 = one pass). Slides are written as overlapping notes, ties as longer notes, accent and normal velocities as set in the plug-in (same rules as "TT-303PATGEN Print to MIDI Item", which must be installed next to this script). PROB and HUMANIZE are not printed.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Prints the pattern of a TT-303PATGEN instance as a real MIDI item, so the live generator becomes a fixed track. Turn on SEQ LINK in TT-303PATGEN first (the script reads the pattern from the gmem namespace tt303pg), select the target track, put the edit cursor where the item should start, run the script and enter the number of bars. Slide is written as overlapping notes, ties as longer notes, accent and normal velocities as set in the plug-in. PROB and HUMANIZE are not printed (the item contains the pattern as written).\par}
}

