{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 TT-303PATGEN\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIDI-only acid pattern generator for REAPER. Generates 303-style patterns (16 to 32 steps, note / octave / gate / tie / accent / slide / probability per step) and plays them as MIDI, synced to the host transport. Accent = velocity above the synth's threshold (default 127 vs. 64, threshold 65 as in the TT-303 1.5.0), slide = overlapping legato notes - exactly what the TT-303 expects in HOST mode, and what any other mono synth understands. Five algorithms (random walk, Markov, Euclid, motif+variation, classic mutation), ten scales plus a custom mask, seeded and reproducible, mutate / rotate / reverse / invert / double, eight pattern slots (A-H), song chain, 32 built-in style patterns plus 16 factory scenes, swing, humanize, MIDI transpose (C2 = original pitch) and an optional gmem link (namespace tt303pg). Operated from the drawn front panel; all parameters stay automatable.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Takes the regions of the project (or, if there are none, the markers) and turns them into the sections of a TT-KNOBMOVER: one section per region / marker, length in whole bars, section type guessed from the name (intro, verse, build, pre, drop, fill, break, outro ...), START BAR set to the bar of the first region. Works on the TT-KNOBMOVER of the first selected track, otherwise the first one in the project. A time selection limits the import to the regions / markers inside it. Undo with Ctrl+Z.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Start this action once (it keeps running in the background, also via a startup action). While it runs, the REGIONS button in the TT-KNOBMOVER header imports the project's regions / markers as sections - the plug-in cannot read project markers itself, this script does it for the instance whose button was pressed. Without the service, run "TT-KNOBMOVER: import regions (or markers) as sections" from the Action list instead. Stop it from the Action list (terminate instances) or by closing REAPER.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 TT-KNOBMOVER\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Rides the knobs of a TT-303 (HOST mode) through a whole track by MIDI CC: cutoff (CC 74), resonance (71), env mod (73), decay (75) and accent (16), optionally volume (7). The song is an arrangement of sections (TEASE, ROLL, BUILD, PRE-DROP, DROP, FILL, BREAK, RESET); every section draws a line from START to END per knob, the cutoff swings on top. Class limits (DRIVER, MELODIC, SCREAM, LOW) act as a guide (green sweet-spot band): untouched sections follow the class table, edited sections and live overrides use the full 0-100 range. Each lane has its own LFO. Notes pass through unchanged. Operated entirely from the drawn front panel.\par}
}

