{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 TT-303 ACID MACHINE \u8212- mono acid synth in the style of the TB-303. Tribute, no samples, no sample ROM, all model.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 CONTROLS AS ON THE ORIGINAL TUNING semitones (-24..+24), plus FINE in cents SLIDE glide time between tied notes, 0..300 ms CUTOFF filter frequency, ~150 Hz .. ~2 kHz exponential (rises with resonance) RESONANCE feedback of the 18 dB ladder up to self-oscillation ENV MOD depth of the filter envelope, up to 5.2 octaves DECAY decay of the filter envelope, ~30 ms .. ~570 ms ACCENT level AND filter boost of the accent circuit WAVEFORM sawtooth / square\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MODEL DETAILS (after R. Whittle / Devil Fish documentation)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Filter: 3-pole ladder (18 dB/oct) in ZDF/TPT form, level-dependent feedback k/(1+0.4|y|), 2x oversampled, then 3-point decimation. Soft clip only at the master, never in the OS loop (it never engages there at real levels anyway).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Pole correction 1/(1+0.10*kRes): mild peak correction; the resonance hump moves up with rising resonance, as on the reference.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Feedback HP 20 Hz IN the feedback path (DC block).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Square with frequency-dependent duty + tilt, classic 1-sample PolyBLEP.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Accent capacitor: recharge +0.95, saturation 1.65. Accent sweep with non-linearity and slight cutoff dependency.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab On accent: fixed 0.2 s filter decay + shortened VCA attack (1.8 ms).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Slide: constant time, log frequency space; the same note stays held.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab FX: delay/reverb bypassed at mix < 0.5 %. EQ OFF = true bypass.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab MIDI: notes are consumed, CC/pitchbend keep going.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 OPERATING MODES HOST Pure sound generator, played from the piano roll. Velocity >= threshold = accent, overlapping notes = slide. The same note again while held is ignored (Devil Fish: the first note-off ends it). Last note wins from a stack of 10 held notes (the oldest falls out); CC 64 (sustain) keeps the gate on while its value is >= 64 (Devil Fish). Accent threshold default 65; the DF button steps through the Devil Fish thresholds 65 / 80 / 100 / 120. SEQ Internal 16-step sequencer, four pattern banks A-D with copy function, random and mutation, shuffle, gate length. Runs on the project timeline or free (FREE RUN). MIDI notes transpose the pattern (C2 = original pitch). MIDI OUT also sends the sequence out. All four banks travel with the project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Effect path: ahead of each of the three units \u8212- WaveShaper (Soft/Hard/ Fold/Fuzz), ping-pong delay, Freeverb reverb \u8212- sits an input EQ as a dual slider (lowcut left, highcut right, 0..20 kHz). After that compressor (-14 dB, 5:1) and master.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The input EQ only shapes what is sent into each effect; the dry signal runs alongside untouched. On the drive what the EQ removes is added back after the WaveShaper, so a raised lowcut takes the bass out of the DISTORTION, not out of the output (drive off = transparent).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 v1.3 (P20): OPTIONS box gains FONT SIZE (FONT 1/2) and a custom HSV colour picker (FONT 1 / FONT 2 / BG) with RESET / RESET ALL, live, per instance, low-contrast warning; dim text contrast raised to WCAG >= 4.5; DSP unchanged.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 v1.3.2 (P23): OPTIONS box: TOOLTIPS ON / OFF (per instance, saved with the project); tooltips on every control (own small mechanism tip303_*, 0.35 s dwell, not while dragging); DSP/audio unchanged.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 v1.3.3 (P25): a slide into the SAME note ties again (no retrigger, one note-on at SEQ OUT), as documented; UNDO restores the bank it was made in; pattern and bank edits create a REAPER undo point; transport start keeps a sounding voice, FX tails, UNDO/COPY and a held transpose key; a tempo re-sync never fires a step twice; mouse wheel = one step on whole-number knobs; test commands need the test unlock.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 PRESETS (v1.2): bar in the header, left of OPTIONS: [<] [name v] [>] [SAVE] [...]. FACTORY (since 2.1.1) = INIT, TT-Groove, TT-BigBoy, TT-HiImTom!, TT-OffbeatBaby, TT-GoodStart (the default presets of the web version, each with its sound and the four pattern banks A-D); USER = 32 slots that travel with the project (@serialize, after the four pattern banks; old projects load with an empty bank). A user preset holds all sound sliders (2..20, 27..32, 34, 35), the pattern settings (length, shuffle, gate, active bank 21/22/23/25) AND the four pattern banks A-D. Not part of it: MODE, FREE RUN, SEQ OUT, MIDI THRU, UI Color, transport. A native REAPER preset file of this plugin carries the whole bank.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIDI: THRU at the top of the header passes INCOMING notes on to the output (CC and pitchbend always pass through anyway). SEQ OUT in the sequencer panel sends the SELF-GENERATED sequence out. Two different sources, hence two switches. In SEQ mode incoming notes are transpose commands \u8212- whoever also passes them on with THRU sends them out next to the sequence.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 SURFACE after the Tim Techlor design kit: Core Black, Core White, Acid Green #39FF14, traces at a 45 degree angle with solder pads. Wordmark in Zilap Orion, if installed. Labels sans-serif (Segoe UI / Helvetica Neue / DejaVu Sans / Arial), numeric values monospaced (Consolas / DejaVu Sans Mono / Menlo / Courier New). Which of these is present the script measures itself. The front computes in a fixed design grid and scales to the window size \u8212- to enlarge, just drag the FX window open. HiDPI is honoured via gfx_ext_retina. All internal JSFX sliders are hidden ("-" before the name), operation is exclusively via the device front.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 TT-KICK Kick Machine v1.1.0\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Kick designer for techno. One kick, three sequential segments on the time axis (TRANSIENT / BODY / TAIL), joined by equal-power crossfades - crossfading instead of layering. Each segment is either SYNTHESIZED or a loaded or captured SAMPLE; the synth path carries its phase across the segment boundaries - phase-coherent by construction, not by offset knobs. The factory state is pure SYNTH on all lanes: a fresh instance plays a complete kick with no kit loaded.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == PLAYING == MIDI: a note-on fires the whole kick chain - TRANSIENT into BODY into TAIL, sequenced on the time axis with equal-power crossfades at the boundaries. Slots left empty drop out of the chain without a click. The note sets the pitch (keytrack base = ROOT, default C2), velocity sets the gain. Note-off is ignored (one-shot). KEYTRACK OFF pins every note to ROOT - factor 1 on any key. DETECT ROOT (player panel) analyzes the BODY segment - loaded sample or rendered synth - and writes ROOT one-shot with the detected note, cent offset and confidence on display. PLAYER: built-in 4/4 player, rate 1/1..1/8, constant velocity; SYNC follows the project timeline (plays while the transport runs), FREE RUN ignores it. SWING delays the off-grid eighths by SWING/200 of an eighth (66.7 % lands on the triplet point). Clicking a lane's waveform auditions that segment - on SYNTH lanes you hear the engine itself. 24 voices; a stolen voice fades out.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == SYNTH ENGINES == Each lane's SYNTH|SAMPLE switch is live. TRANSIENT renders a click oscillator + noise burst, BODY a pitch-envelope oscillator (f0 -> f1, curve-shaped), TAIL a sine with drift and a room component. Chained synth segments share one phase trajectory: a successor starts at the exact phase its predecessor holds at the boundary - no phase jump inside or across the crossfade. The chain's phase starts at 0; a synth segment following a SAMPLE segment also starts at phase 0. Lane length sets the synth window duration (per-type maximum); PITCH and the played note scale the engine frequencies.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == EDITING == Each lane carries its segment window: drag the START/LENGTH flags to trim, drag the diamond markers at the window edges to set the crossfade lengths (the end fade on TAIL is the kick's fade-out), REV flips the window, GAIN sets the segment level. Every lane has its own zoom: - / + zoom out and in, FIT (ZOOM FIT) makes the view follow the lane window, a scroll bar under the wave moves the zoomed view. Mouse wheel over a waveform = zoom at the pointer, CTRL+wheel = scroll, SHIFT+wheel = vertical skew, dragging the dimmed background pans the zoomed view. Presets store the zoom; factory and lane presets open with ZOOM FIT on every lane. Vertical lines with ms labels sit behind every waveform. Edits while a kick plays apply to the next trigger - running voices are frozen at trigger time, so drags never stutter. Hover any control for a short hint (OPTIONS -> TOOLTIPS ON/OFF). CTRL+click resets a fader, flag, diamond or knob to its INIT value.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == LANE TOOLS == M / S take a lane out of the kick chain (mute) or leave only soloed lanes in it. MAX blows one lane up to fill the whole lane area (the others collapse to strips). RAND draws a fresh, musically bounded random setting for the lane (CTRL+click = INIT). EXPERT opens a row of knobs under every lane: the engine knobs (F0, F1 with the nearest note, e.g. F0 A4 = 440 Hz, and NOISE / CURVE / DRIFT + ROOM), PITCH, LEN, OFFSET, XF-IN, XF-OUT and a LANE FILTER (CUT / RES, a 2-pole low-pass on that lane's voices only; fully open it is bypassed bit-exactly). XF-IN and XF-OUT are independent: a boundary fades over min(XF-OUT of the earlier lane, XF-IN of the later lane). OFFSET moves the start of a lane on the time axis, in ms with 0.1 ms steps. Without it a lane starts where the one before ends, minus the shared crossfade. A positive OFFSET starts it later and leaves a gap of silence between the lanes, a negative OFFSET starts it earlier and overlaps the lanes more (S2 / S3: -100..+100 ms). On S1 (the head of the chain) a positive OFFSET (0..+100 ms) delays the whole kick. Every lane after a moved lane moves with it. At 0 on all lanes the kick is exactly the same as before. In the WAVE page and in FUSION EXPAND a grip at the foot of each lane start drags OFFSET sideways (double-click or CTRL+click = 0). Every lane header carries a preset browser < NAME >: INIT plus 14 curated entries per lane (S1 transient, S2 body, S3 tail). A lane preset sets only the 16 sound parameters; window, view, MUTE / SOLO stay. A "*" marks a sound edited after loading.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == WAVE VIEW == The kick is shown as its real waveform, rendered from the lanes before the master section (filter, drive, clip and OUT are not in it) at velocity 127. The preview renders silently in the background after every edit; no hit is needed and the sound is unchanged. S1 / S2 / S3 carry their own colours, derived from the OPTIONS colour scheme.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Lane boxes: ENV / WAVE / BOTH in every lane header. ENV = the curves, WAVE = the rendered wave of this lane, BOTH = both (default). A muted lane shows its wave dimmed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab FUSION: the row below the lanes shows the assembled kick and its total length. SUM = the finished kick as one wave, coloured by the loudest lane; STACK = one row per lane at its real place in the kick plus the sum. EXPAND lets FUSION fill the lane area: drag the END flags (lane length) and the diamonds (crossfade between two lanes, end fade) right in the wave; click plays the kick, click on a STACK row plays that lane, OPEN jumps to the lane. Each lane shows DUR against its recommended range (REC): green = inside, orange = outside.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab FIT LENGTH TO / FIT NOW (FUSION header): scales the playing lanes once, in proportion, so the kick lasts a chosen note length (1/1 .. 1/16 incl. triplets) at the current tempo. AUTO (saved per instance) fits after every preset load, in the same undo step.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab WAVE page (header tab): the whole kick on one time line with the next player hit as a red line, SUM or LAYERS, a LUPE for the first 20 ms, wheel zoom, SHIFT+wheel scroll, overview strip and FIT. Below sits the selected lane with its controls and the EXPERT knob row, plus that lane alone on its own time scale. All view switches are saved per instance and never create undo steps; the edits in the wave are normal, undoable edits.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == CAPTURE == Each lane has a CAP button (next to REV): record incoming audio straight into that lane's sample slot - no file dialog, no disk. Click CAP (lane shows "REC ARMED - PLAY YOUR SOURCE"), then play the source into the plugin's audio input (track input or items before this FX). Recording starts when the mono input exceeds -40 dB for 3 samples in a row, stops after 8 s, or after 1 s of silence (min. 0.2 s recorded); the silent tail is trimmed. Click CAP again on the armed/recording lane = ABORT (discard). On commit the lane switches to SAMPLE automatically. Outside an armed or running capture the input is not passed through. Captured slots are VOLATILE: they survive kit reloads (other slots reloading does not touch them; a new path assigned to that very slot replaces the capture), but NOT a sample-rate change and NOT a project reload - they are never written to the project. Bounce the result to a WAV if you want to keep it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == LOADING SAMPLES == The front has no file dialogs (JSFX limitation). Run a Lua loader script ("TT-KICK Load Kit", "(Folder)", "(from Items)"; Actions -> Load ReaScript): it assigns the WAVs to the slots (TRANSIENT / BODY / TAIL) and hands the kit to ONE TT-KICK instance - the TT-KICK window that has (or last had) the focus, otherwise the first TT-KICK on the selected track; every instance can carry its own kit. Cancelling a dialog keeps the current slot assignment; a path longer than 255 characters is rejected with a message. The paths travel with the project - after a reload the WAVs are pulled from the stored paths again. "TT-KICK Recent Kits" re-loads a kit folder from a menu. Scripts can also hand lane sounds (lane preset format) to one instance through the hidden "Lane request (Lua)" parameter (one undo step).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == MASTER CHAIN == The summed kick runs through four rack stages on the right: FILTER - resonant LP (two TPT state-variable stages); BEEF biases the resonance peak up to 3 octaves BELOW the cutoff. DRIVE - BEEF is a parallel bass-band drive: the band is shaped while the remainder passes the BEEF stage undistorted (PUNCH PROTECT; switch it off to drive the full signal). GLUE is a sum saturation on top and deliberately touches the remainder too - bit-exact transparency therefore needs BEEF=0 AND GLUE=0. CLIP - soft/hard clipper with ceiling (the SOFT/HARD selector is dimmed while CLIP is off). OUT - gain plus peak/RMS metering, scope below. Every switch and fader rides on a ~20 ms slew - no step ever reaches the audio, stages keep tracking the signal while bypassed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == PRESETS / UNDO / SYSTEM == Header row 2, left of OPTIONS: [<] [ name v ] [>] [SAVE] [...]. The dropdown lists FACTORY (INIT + 44 kicks in eight families: 909 / 808 / HARD / RUMBLE / MINIMAL / DEEP / ROLL / CHAR, all pure synth, license-free) and USER (32 slots). A preset writes the full state (all lane and segment data, master chain, player head) and keeps the kit paths; a factory preset keeps your ROOT note, INIT resets it to C2. SAVE stores everything a factory preset replaces (not kit paths, colour, lane view, player ON, page). The user bank rides in the project and in every native REAPER preset of this plugin (+ button). "*" = edited. UNDO (header + SYSTEM page) walks back the last 20 edit states: a snapshot is pushed when a drag ends or a button edit lands; each step also marks the REAPER project as changed. SYSTEM holds the factory preset families, the undo depth readout, live MIDI/SYNC status and build info. EXPORT: run "TT-KICK Export Kick.lua" from the action list - it renders the kick over 4 bars (or the current time selection) into an item named TTKICK_.wav on the selected track.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == OPTIONS == The OPTIONS button in the header opens a box with ten colour schemes (ACID = factory, CYAN, ORANGE, MAGENTA, YELLOW, RED, BLUE, VIOLET, MINT, ICE), font size, custom colours, UI SIZE (25..400 %), AUTO FIT ON/OFF (the UI zoom follows the window size) and TOOLTIPS ON/OFF. Everything is stored per plugin instance and saved with the project; presets, RAND and undo never touch it.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 TT-RUMBLER Rumble Machine v1.1.0\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Techno rumble machine - part of the TimTechlor line (TT-303 Acid Machine = bass, Kick = the kick, TT-RUMBLER = the rumble under it). It builds the pumping sub-bass layer from the kick signal sitting right before it in the FX chain (e.g. Kick) - Kikzilla-Lite-style chain, fully open parameters, plus a PITCH engine no Kikzilla has.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == SIGNAL FLOW == In -> trigger detect -> [DRY: KICK fader] + [ENGINE (VERB | NOISE | PITCH) -> AHDR gate -> LOW CUT -> DRIVE -> HIGH CUT + ENV DEPTH -> auto gain -> RUMBLE fader] -> sum -> clipper -> OUT. The engines run on the mono mid signal; the rumble output is mono duplicated to L/R, the dry kick stays stereo.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == TRIGGER == AUDIO follows the input peak (0.5 ms attack / 50 ms release) with ~3 dB hysteresis and a 30 ms debounce. TRIGGER = AUDIO / AUDIO+MIDI / MIDI: note-ons can fire the envelope as well (sample-accurate via block queue).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == ENVELOPE == START / ATTACK / HOLD / RELEASE are independent times in ms. START is a pure delay before the attack, so the rumble swells after the kick punch instead of eating it. CURVE shapes attack and release (p = 2^(3*c), -500 -> 0.125, +500 -> 8). FIT TO scales the four durations once to a note at the current tempo; later tempo changes never rescale the stored times.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == ENGINES == VERB - 4 feedback combs + damping + 2 allpasses (MODAL / WALL / BLOOM), DECAY = T60 (nominal - loop damping shortens the tail at low FOCUS), FOCUS = damping pivot 40..400 Hz, DENSE = diffusion. NOISE - LCG noise (CLASSIC 3x one-pole cascade / GRIT clipped / RUBBLE bandpass), TONE = colour. PITCH - the kick itself through a 32768-sample ring, v0.8.0: cubic read-head interpolation; a window change also updates the playback rate in the same sample. Discrete engine, character and cut-type switches have a 5 ms click guard. two read heads, Hann half-period crossfade, 0..-24 st (whole semitones since v0.6.0). Characters TIGHT / DEEP / GRAIN scale the window x0.5 / x1 / x2. Inherent latency is ~W/2 samples (about 21-85 ms at 48 kHz, by character); the envelope restart is delayed by the same amount and the window phase locks to each kick onset, so gate and shifted tail stay aligned and deterministic. Since v0.9.2 the dry kick is delayed by the same engine latency and reported to the host (PDC), so kick and rumble start together (LATENCY AUTO / FIXED).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == OPTIONS / COLOR == OPTIONS button in the header (right of the preset bar) opens a box with 10 colour schemes (accent, second colour, tinted ground); per plugin instance, saved with the project, not touched by presets or UNDO. Factory scheme: ACID. v0.5.0: the box also carries FONT SIZE steps and a custom colour picker (FONT 1 / FONT 2 / BG) - saved per instance as well. v0.5.4: OPTIONS > TOOLTIPS ON / OFF is the one tooltip switch (the TIPS switch in the header is gone; older projects keep their setting).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == PRESET BAR / USER BANK (v0.4.0) == Header bar left of OPTIONS: [<] [name v] [>] [SAVE] [...]. The dropdown lists FACTORY (INIT + the 21 factory presets) and USER (32 slots, kept in the plugin state: project, FX chain, track template and every native REAPER preset file). A preset = the 28 sound parameters (not KICK/RUMBLE switches, colour, tips). Loading a preset can be undone with UNDO.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == SCOPE / TEMPO (v0.7.0) == The scope at the top draws the incoming KICK (white) and the RUMBLE (accent colour) together on one scale, optionally the SUM (final output) and the envelope GATE line, with the gate windows (A/H/R) of every LENGTH cycle drawn as bands. FIXED holds one bar still while a cursor redraws it, ROLL scrolls (left = oldest). Bar length follows the host time signature. The trace and view switches are display settings only (not saved, no undo point). The row under the scope shows the host BPM and the length of 1/2, 1/4 and 1/8 notes in ms and Hz (ms = 60000 / BPM x beats, Hz = 1000 / ms).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == FILTER / MIX == MIX: the KICK / RUMBLE switches left of the faders mute (lit = audible); off mutes only the output (soft ramp), the trigger, engine and AUTO GAIN keep running. Not stored in presets. LOW CUT resonant HP, DRIVE parallel band (~140 Hz), HIGH CUT CLEAN / COMB / DIRTY with ENV DEPTH opening it up to 4 octaves, AUTO GAIN (feed-forward peak-hold, rumble ~6 dB under the kick, freezes in breakdowns), clipper with ceiling + clip LED, OUT +-12 dB and a +-2.0 safety clamp behind it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == STATE / MILESTONES == v0.1.0 is feature-complete (M1-M5): the 66-word parameter blob rides @serialize (v3 since 0.9.0: magic + version + 64 words), a 20-slot undo ring (up to 19 edits) lives in memory, and INIT + 21 factory presets (8 VERB / 7 NOISE / 6 PITCH, designed in the tt-rumbler_lab.py transcript) sit in the header preset bar (v0.4.0). Every panel parameter is a draggable widget with tooltips. v0.5.4: every edit (drag, wheel, reset, switch, colour, preset load, UNDO) is reported to REAPER - one undo point, project marked as changed.\par}
}

